        "One unit consists of two flotation cells: the first cell is a Suctionslot and the second is an Directslot, with an intermediate chamber between them. Air is sucked in through the air inlet pipe with relatively large air intake. Nevertheless, as an older‑design machine, the XJ‑Type delivers uneven air dispersion, unstable froth and tends to cause splashing. Liquid‑level control is difficult to realize.",
